definition.message:
{{#is_alert}}
Dell PowerFlex protection domain {{protection_domain_name.name}} (ID: {{protection_domain_id.name}}) has {{value}} KB of failed capacity.

This means one or more storage devices or SDS nodes have failed. The cluster is operating in a degraded state and may not tolerate additional failures.

Investigate immediately:
- Check SDS node health and connectivity.
- Verify device error counts (`dell_powerflex.num_dev_errors`).
- Monitor rebuild progress (`dell_powerflex.norm_rebuild_write_bwc.*`).
- Confirm the MDM cluster state is healthy.
{{/is_alert}}

{{#is_recovery}}
Failed capacity in Dell PowerFlex protection domain {{protection_domain_name.name}} has been resolved. Rebuild may have completed successfully.
{{/is_recovery}}
